From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dynamic Devices <opensource@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
Date: Mon, 1 Sep 2026 16:40:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] waylandsink: fix runtime rank registration

GST_ELEMENT_REGISTER_DEFINE expands to a function definition and therefore
cannot be used inside plugin_init.  The NXP fork moved it into plugin_init so
that the rank could be selected at runtime, which Clang correctly rejects.

Register the element directly instead.  This preserves the NXP runtime rank
selection without defining a function inside another function.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Dynamic Devices <opensource@dynamicdevices.co.uk>
---
 ext/wayland/gstwaylandsink.c | 6 ++----
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/ext/wayland/gstwaylandsink.c b/ext/wayland/gstwaylandsink.c
index 2158cfcaa3..e69cb14fc8 100644
--- a/ext/wayland/gstwaylandsink.c
+++ b/ext/wayland/gstwaylandsink.c
@@ -1495,10 +1495,8 @@ plugin_init (GstPlugin * plugin)
   if (imx_chip_code() >= CC_MX8)
       rank = IMX_GST_PLUGIN_RANK + 1;
 
-  GST_ELEMENT_REGISTER_DEFINE (waylandsink, "waylandsink", rank,
-    GST_TYPE_WAYLAND_SINK);
-
-  return GST_ELEMENT_REGISTER (waylandsink, plugin);
+  return gst_element_register (plugin, "waylandsink", rank,
+      GST_TYPE_WAYLAND_SINK);
 }
 
 GST_PLUGIN_DEFINE (GST_VERSION_MAJOR,
-- 
